§ `Dates for the Charter of Human Rights and Responsibilities Act 2006`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- s 2(1): "This Charter (except Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3) comes into operation on 1 January 2007." Part 2 (the
-- rights) commences that day; s 49(2) counts from it.
`the day Part 2 came into operation` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2007

-- s 2(2): "Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3 come into operation on 1 January 2008." Division 3 is ss 32-37 (interpretation),
-- Division 4 is ss 38-39 (public authorities, legal proceedings); the endnotes agree ("sections 32-39 on 1 January
-- 2008"). s 49(3) counts from it.
`the day Divisions 3 and 4 of Part 3 came into operation` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2008

-- A Gregorian leap year.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

-- s 31(7): "the 5th anniversary of the day on which that provision comes into operation". The same day and month five
-- years on; for 29 February, when the fifth year is not a leap year, 28 February (fork F9 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 5th anniversary of` `the start` MEANS
    IF     (DATE_DAY `the start` EQUALS 29)
       AND (DATE_MONTH `the start` EQUALS 2)
       AND (NOT (`leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS 5)))
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS 5)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the start`) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) (DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS 5)
